<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms clears CGE buy of UK rail firm.</title>
<headline>EU confirms clears CGE buy of UK rail firm.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had approved the acquisition by Compagnie Generale d'Entreprises Automobiles, which belongs to French utility giant CGE, of British passenger rail firm South Eastern Train Ltd.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the deal would not risk to create or strengthen a dominant position.</p>
<p>The operation is part of the privatisation of British Railways, which formerly owned South Eastern.</p>
<p>In May, the EU also cleared CGEA's purchase of Network SouthCentral Ltd another British Railways's former unit. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
